{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30129 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Alpha-Cedrene epoxide is implicated in the targeting of Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that alpha-Cedrene epoxide acts as a target for multiple compounds, including HaCaT, SF-188, and MOVP-3, which in turn target Replicase polyprotein 1ab. This indicates a potential mechanism where alpha-Cedrene epoxide may interact with these compounds, which then exert their effects on Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The presence of multiple pathways linking alpha-Cedrene epoxide to Replicase polyprotein 1ab suggests a broader role in the biological process, possibly involving the modulation of viral replication. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that alpha-Cedrene epoxide may influence viral replication through a series of intermediate targets, thereby supporting a role in the pathogenesis or regulation of viral processes.",
